    thread_5_summary:Cross-x amortisation across the three pillars. Galway/Connes obstruction (Thread 3) is per-query, but Riemann zeros are properties of zeta not x. If K zeros are computed once and reused across M queries pi(x_1)..pi(x_M), per-x amortised cost decomposes into K_zeros_setup (amortisable) + K_per_x_evaluation (not). Question: can K_per_x_evaluation be polylog(x) while K_zeros_setup = Theta-tilde(x_max)? Same question for Meissel-Lehmer/HKM intermediate-sieve sharing across x. And: Aggarwal binary search makes O(log x) sub-queries to pi(.) at different x values - is there missed amortisation in the Aggarwal analysis? S202 WRAP explicitly listed cross-x amortisation as a "legitimate falsifier of Thread 3, noted as open but not needed for Thread 2 closure." This thread closes that falsifier.
    thread_5_a_grade_targets:(a) per-x amortised polylog over M = poly(log x_max) batched queries (paper-grade, batch-polylog π(x) algorithm); (b) Aggarwal analysis was sub-optimal — improved binary search via amortisation (concrete algorithmic speedup); (c) cross-x lower bound matching empirical curve under Montgomery (extends Thread 3 closure).
